2026-07-24T14:18:42.3249121Z               "message": "Fix legacy config-revision 404 + config UI polish\n\nBackend\n- ConfigService now migrates pre-split revision history on load. Revisions\n  saved before the history-storage split (bodies embedded inline in\n  config-history.json, no per-revision files) 404'd because GetRevision only\n  looked for config-rev-{id}.json. LoadHistory externalises each inline body to\n  its own file and collapses the index to the body-less format — one-time,\n  idempotent, and skipped if any body fails to write so nothing is lost.\n- Regression test covers listing + loading legacy inline revisions and the\n  index rewrite.\n\nConfig UI\n- Messages are now a fixed overlay toast instead of an in-flow block, so\n  showing/hiding no longer reflows the page (fixes the \"jumpy\" feel). Success\n  auto-dismisses after 4s; warnings/errors persist until dismissed or replaced\n  and gain a close control.\n- Per-domain DKIM selectors panel is now collapsible (open by default) with a\n  live entry-count hint.\n- Added spacing below the form action buttons so they no longer butt against\n  the Maintenance section.\n- Added floating scroll-to-top / scroll-to-bottom controls for the long page.\n- Nav: \"API docs\" -> \"API\" with a new-tab indicator; \"Tokens\" -> \"Access\n  Tokens\" across the validator, tokens and config pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
