2026-07-24T14:18:42.3270006Z               "message": "Filter revision history to revisions with an existing body file\n\nReplace the pre-split inline-body migration with a simpler read filter, per\ndeployment reality: on the one deployed instance the legacy inline bodies were\nalready dropped when config-history.json was first rewritten body-less, so the\nolder revisions are unrecoverable and only their metadata remains.\n\nListRevisions now returns only revisions whose config-rev-{id}.json exists, so\nthe picker never offers a revision whose body is gone (which loaded as a 404).\nGetRevision already returns null for a missing body; the filter keeps the UI\nfrom ever reaching that path.\n\nTest updated to assert an orphaned revision (metadata without a body file) is\nexcluded from the listing while the rest still load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
