2026-07-24T14:18:42.3281953Z               "message": "Fix encrypted keyring decryption + clean up plaintext keys on startup\n\nTwo related data-protection keyring fixes for distributed (Redis) mode where\nthe ring lives on a shared mount and can be encrypted at rest:\n\n- Decryptor activation: DataProtection instantiates the IXmlDecryptor named in\n  an encrypted key via its own activator, which in some hosting paths runs\n  without the DI container and calls a parameterless constructor. SecretXmlDecryptor\n  only had a (DataProtectionSecret) constructor, so activation threw\n  MissingMethodException — every encrypted key became ineligible and SSO 500'd.\n  Add a parameterless constructor that recovers an ambient secret published at\n  startup. End-to-end test protects then unprotects across a simulated restart\n  with the secret absent from DI, forcing the activator/ambient path.\n\n- Plaintext cleanup: when DataProtection:KeyEncryptionSecret is configured,\n  remove any unencrypted key files at startup so the next key request writes a\n  fresh encrypted key. DP only encrypts newly generated keys and never\n  re-encrypts an existing plaintext key, so otherwise a plaintext key lingers on\n  the shared mount until it expires. Dropping keys only invalidates active OIDC\n  sessions (users re-authenticate); the token cookie is not data-protected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
