2026-07-24T14:18:42.3290376Z               "id": "5acc7b292efd7b621c4fe85f6ecdd6add37239ce",
2026-07-24T14:18:42.3293889Z               "message": "Clear the shared Redis L2 on cache-clear; fix Maintenance warning layout\n\nCache clear in distributed mode was ineffective: ClearAllAsync wiped only the\ncalling pod's in-memory L1 and the on-disk cache, leaving the shared Redis L2\n(cache:* keys) intact — so the cleared pod refilled from stale L2 entries at\nonce and other pods kept their own L1. It looked like a no-op cluster-wide.\n\n- RedisConnection.DeleteKeysByPrefixAsync scans and deletes keys by prefix via\n  SCAN (no admin mode; never FLUSHDB, so jobs and beacons survive).\n- CacheManager takes the Redis handle and, on ClearAllAsync, also clears the\n  shared probe-cache L2 (cache:). Other replicas' L1 still expires on its own TTL.\n- Maintenance copy updated to describe memory + disk + shared Redis accurately.\n\nUI: the Maintenance warning box had gone askew because the toast redesign made\n.msg a flexbox, so this static .msg.warn block laid its text and the inline\n<strong> out as separate flex items. Scope the flex/overlay styling to\n#messages .msg so the standalone warning flows as normal inline text again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
