2026-07-24T14:18:42.3310456Z               "message": "Clean up expired data-protection keys at startup\n\nDataProtection generates a new key ~every 90 days but never removes expired\nones, so on a long-lived shared mount old key-*.xml files accumulate.\n\n- DataProtectionKeyring.RemoveStaleKeys deletes key files whose <expirationDate>\n  is older than a retention window; keys that are unexpired (incl. the active\n  key), expired but within the window, or have no parseable expiry are kept.\n- Startup wires it up via DataProtection:KeyRetentionDays (default 30), floored\n  at the max OIDC session lifetime + 1 day so a key that could still unprotect a\n  live session cookie is never deleted regardless of the configured value. Runs\n  before the provider reads the ring, so DP never references a removed key.\n- Tests cover long-expired vs recent/active/undated keys and malformed/missing\n  inputs. horizontal-scaling.md documents the setting and housekeeping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
